course: dictionary
lesson: 7866
title: One word, two meanings: rainbow
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. The first meaning of rainbow is a curved band of colours in the sky. «A prism splits white light into the colours of the rainbow.» Here the colours are bands of light, so rainbow means the colours that light makes.
explain: The second meaning is for things, not the sky. Rainbow can describe anything with many bright colours in bands, like a rainbow scarf. When you meet a word twice, check which meaning your sentence needs.
explain: A rainbow is always a little out of reach. «A rainbow is light, not a thing in one place, so you can never walk to the end of a rainbow: it moves as you move.» That is why «at the end of the rainbow» is a story idea, not a real place you can visit.
fact: A rainbow is a curved band of colours in the sky, made when sunlight shines through raindrops.
fact: «A rainbow has 7 colours, a clock face 12 numbers and a compass 4 main points.»
fact: «A prism splits white light into the colours of the rainbow.»
fact: Rainbow can also describe anything with many bright colours in bands, like a rainbow scarf.
fact: In stories, a rainbow is often a sign of hope after a storm.
exercise: «A prism splits white light into the colours of the rainbow.» What does rainbow mean here? | A storm with thunder | A type of cloud | *The band of colours that light makes | A bird with bright feathers
exercise: «She wore a rainbow scarf with stripes of red, blue and green.» What does rainbow mean here? | A loud noise | A rain shower in the park | *Bright colours in bands, not a sky | A curved band in the sky
exercise: «A rainbow has 7 colours, a clock face 12 numbers and a compass 4 main points.» How many colours does a rainbow have? | 12 | 4 | *7 | 3
test: Why can you never walk to the end of a rainbow? | Because the end is too far away to see | *Because a rainbow is light and moves as you move | Because rainbows only appear at night | Because the rainbow is made of stone
test: In stories, what does a rainbow often show? | A sign that school is closed | Cold weather ahead | *Hope after a storm | A dark cloud coming
exam: Lena says, «A rainbow is something you can fetch from the garden.» Is she right, and why? | *No, a rainbow is light, so it cannot be picked up | Yes, but only in summer | Yes, rainbows grow in gardens | Yes, it sits on the ground after rain
